# `#524` REPAIR-CHAIN PASS — the detector repair made in response to pass 2 owes its own pass

VERDICT line first, then the liveness token `CODEX_524REPAIR_20260911`.

## Why this pass exists, and what would END the chain

This project's rule: **a repair made in response to a pass 2 OWES ITS OWN PASS 2** — the obligation
follows the MATERIAL, not the narrative. The stop condition is **one pass per floor-bound diff,
closing on the FIRST PASS THAT FINDS ZERO FLOOR BREACHES**. A bare "no breaches" does NOT close it;
**a zero closes only WITH ITS DENOMINATOR — which cells, which mutant shapes, you actually swept.**

**Review EFFORT is scoped to the repair diff below. The FLOOR QUESTION — does a clean-sweep mutant
exist in the clause-(d) enumeration — is asked of the SHIPPED COMPOSITE every pass.**

**Do not ratify.** Seven times today a pass has refuted a premise of mine, every time correctly.
**"This repair is defective" is the most valuable answer you can give**, and this project has a
measured case where exactly this kind of repair reproduced the original breach at the symmetric
site.

