18051: A5.1.3 Data-processing operands - Immediate
18052: 
18053:       31  28 27 26 25 24  21 20 19  16 15                      12 11  87                      0
18054: 
18055:           cond 0 0 1 opcode S Rn             Rd rotate_imm                           immed_8
18056: 
18057:       This data-processing operand provides a constant (defined in the instruction) operand to a data-processing
18058:       instruction.
18059: 
18060:       The <shifter_operand> value is formed by rotating (to the right) an 8-bit immediate value to any even bit
18061:       position in a 32-bit word. If the rotate immediate is zero, the carry-out from the shifter is the value of the C
18062:       flag, otherwise, it is set to bit[31] of the value of <shifter_operand>.
18063: 
18064:       Syntax          Specifies the immediate constant wanted. It is encoded in the instruction as an 8-bit
18065:                       immediate (immed_8) and a 4-bit immediate (rotate_imm), so that <immediate> is
18066:       #<immediate>    equal to the result of rotating immed_8 right by (2 x rotate_imm) bits.
18067: 
18068:       where:
18069: 
18070:       <immediate>
18071: 
18072:       Operation
18073: 
18074:       shifter_operand = immed_8 Rotate_Right (rotate_imm * 2)
18075:       if rotate_imm == 0 then
18076: 
18077:             shifter_carry_out = C flag
18078:       else /* rotate_imm != 0 */
18079: 
18080:             shifter_carry_out = shifter_operand[31]
