19747: A5.4.2 Load and Store Multiple - Increment after
19748: 
19749: 31             28 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 19  16 15                                       0
19750: 
19751:                cond 1 0 0 0 1 S W L Rn                             register list
19752: 
19753: This addressing mode is for Load and Store Multiple instructions, and forms a range of addresses.
19754: 
19755: The first address formed is the <start_address>, and is the value of the base register Rn. Subsequent
19756: addresses are formed by incrementing the previous address by four. One address is produced for each
19757: register that is specified in <registers>.
19758: 
19759: The last address produced is the <end_address>. Its value is four less than the sum of the value of the base
19760: register and four times the number of registers specified in <registers>.
19761: 
19762: If the condition specified in the instruction matches the condition code status and the W bit is set, Rn is
19763: incremented by four times the number of registers in <registers>. The conditions are defined in The
19764: condition field on page A3-3.
19765: 
19766: Syntax
19767: 
19768: IA
19769: 
19770: See also the alternative syntax described in Load and Store Multiple addressing modes (alternative names)
19771: on page A5-47.
19772: 
19773: Operation
19774: 
19775: start_address = Rn
19776: end_address = Rn + (Number_Of_Set_Bits_In(register_list) * 4) - 4
19777: if ConditionPassed(cond) and W == 1 then
19778: 
19779:       Rn = Rn + (Number_Of_Set_Bits_In(register_list) * 4)
19780: 
19781: Notes          This bit distinguishes between a Load Multiple and a Store Multiple.
19782: The L bit
