1623: 
1624: Reading the program counter
1625: 
1626: When an instruction reads the PC, the value read depends on which instruction set it comes from:
1627: 
1628: � For an ARM instruction, the value read is the address of the instruction plus 8 bytes. Bits [1:0] of this
1629:         value are always zero, because ARM instructions are always word-aligned.
1630: 
1631: � For a Thumb instruction, the value read is the address of the instruction plus 4 bytes. Bit [0] of this
1632:         value is always zero, because Thumb instructions are always halfword-aligned.
