8200: A4.1.23 LDR
8201: 
8202: 31             28 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 19  16 15      12 11                            0
8203: 
8204:                cond 0 1 I P U 0 W 1 Rn               Rd                  addr_mode
8205: 
8206: LDR (Load Register) loads a word from a memory address.
8207: 
8208: If the PC is specified as register <Rd>, the instruction loads a data word which it treats as an address, then
8209: branches to that address. In ARMv5T and above, bit[0] of the loaded value determines whether execution
8210: continues after this branch in ARM state or in Thumb state, as though a BX (loaded_value) instruction had
8211: been executed. In earlier versions of the architecture, bits[1:0] of the loaded value are ignored and execution
8212: continues in ARM state, as though a MOV PC,(loaded_value) instruction had been executed.
8213: 
